short_label: XI.37
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If four straight lines are proportional, then parallelepipedal solids on them which are similar and similarly described are also proportional; and, if the parallelepipedal solids on them which are similar and similarly described are proportional, then the straight lines themselves are also proportional.
----
proof:

Let *AB, CD, EF,* and *GH* be four straight lines in proportion, so that *AB* is to *CD* as *EF* is to *GH,* and let there be described on *AB, CD, EF,* and *GH* the similar and similarly situated parallelepipedal solids *KA, LC, ME, NG.*

I say that *KA* is to *LC* as *ME* is to *NG.*

